#################################################################

ex:requiresCapability rdfs:comment "Process class -> the capability an agent must bear to perform it. DERIVED from ex:enablesProcess (author scope once on the capability; generate this inverse onto the process, so the two never drift -- PHASE1 §8). Intended domain: a process universal (reaches obo:BFO_0000015); intended range: a class reaching cco:ont00001379 Agent Capability (an Organization Capability cco:ont00000568 qualifies, since 568 ⊑ 1379). Matching is species-satisfies-genus: an agent bearing C_a satisfies a requirement C_p iff C_a rdfs:subClassOf* C_p. Range enforced by SHACL C5." ;
                      rdfs:label "requires capability" .


ex:requiresRole rdfs:comment "Process class -> the role in whose capacity the work must be performed. Intended domain: a process universal; intended range: a class reaching obo:BFO_0000023 Role (typically a cco:ont00000984 Occupation Role or cco:ont00000187 Authority Role). Same species-satisfies-genus matching as ex:requiresCapability. Range enforced by SHACL C6." ;
                rdfs:label "requires role" .


